  "reference_notes": "Inspected the Oxford woodland photograph and RHS close-up of English bluebells, then all three current pilots and 36 variants. Replaced oversize radial flower stars with small attached pendulous tubular corollas along the outer side of the bent raceme. Basal strap leaves and uncluttered upright flower stalks retain the characteristic habit. All 36 silhouettes span 0.17-0.35 m. At 25 mm the real 15-25 mm corollas necessarily merge into a few purple cells, especially in compact small variants; curled tepal lips cannot resolve. Accepted as a stylized spring English bluebell source with this explicit resolution limit. User seed endorsement remains separate.",
